      "rationale": "This guarded base equation defines the value of the new mathematical summary largestDivisorAtOrBelow when D is a positive divisor of N; it matches no operational configuration and was present in VERIFICATION before all Stage 1 proof runs.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-0f02393212bfcf7e7c8810a806f9829aa2bbf9b5bd9795c9a7b5db26160d7995",
      "start_line": 10,
      "text": "  rule largestDivisorAtOrBelow(N, D) => D\n    requires D >=Int 1\n     andBool pyMod(N, D) ==Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 17,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "99644c7600e08ea07b0c26314084adf2ab5eb468a6b1eb4aadd857b2f427b14a",
      "rationale": "This guarded recurrence defines the descending-search case of largestDivisorAtOrBelow by reducing D to D -Int 1 when D is not a divisor; it matches no operational configuration and was present in VERIFICATION before all Stage 1 proof runs.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-99644c7600e08ea07b0c26314084adf2ab5eb468a6b1eb4aadd857b2f427b14a",
      "start_line": 14,
      "text": "  rule largestDivisorAtOrBelow(N, D)\n    => largestDivisorAtOrBelow(N, D -Int 1)\n    requires D >Int 1\n     andBool pyMod(N, D) =/=Int 0"
    }
